A||||12||DISenchanted||Realy tough Decision.||||5||
Z||000000||DISenchanted||01-14-2000||04:24 AM||||Ok here it is.  I have a chance to sell my 85 gt for $1700.  It's not in the greatest shape, but I have turned it into a very reliable car.  While searching through the classifieds, I found it.  An 87 gt for only 1500 dollars.  What luck.  Well, I went and looked at it today.  I found out a few things that bother me.  First off, it has a salvaged title.  Not too pleased at that.  It needs a new paint job, and the front hood seems out of alignment.  The water pump is bad, and the drivers seat is pretty bad too.  The car sounded great though.  I talked with the owner and he said that he'd change the seats with a pair or mint 85 seats.  He also said that he'd fix the water pump.  After talking a while longer, I checked the computer and it gave me a code 32?  None of the guages seem to work right either.  He said he'd give it to me for $1300.  Should I do it?  And TOM are you busy next week?  I was wondering if I could borrow you, or any one else in Southern California, to take a look at it with me.  It's located in North Hollywood.<P>Thank you for your time.||||reg||5
Z||000001||fiero56||01-14-2000||08:38 AM||||Code 32 is an EGR system code. It could be several things(valve,solonoid, vaccume lines,EGR tube, etc.)<BR>$1700 for a GT with these problems seems a might steep. $1300 is even a little high. What is the mileage on the car? I'm sure you can find a little better for the same amount. Make sure there is no frame damage(especially check the front) since you say not all the body panels line up.<BR>No matter what you buy and what you pay, there will always be a better deal going on somewhere. I paid less than $1300 for my Formula, and it was in excellent condition. Even after I bought the car, I was still checking the classifieds to see if there was a Fiero for even a better deal.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||TOM||01-14-2000||10:27 AM||||I would be happy to go with you and check out the car. Maybe if we do the pump we can talk him down a bit more.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ggarsk||01-14-2000||11:09 AM||||The thing that would make me really wonder about that car is the salvage title. Was it in a big accident...in a flood or what? ||||reg||1
Z||000004||DISenchanted||01-14-2000||12:28 PM||||Ok, there is 130,000 on the odometer.  The car was suposedly hit in the front drivers side. The pannels line up, but the hood looks like its not on straight.  He said he had to take it off.  He said the reason for the salvaged title, is because he got it from a Salvation Army auction.  And he said that they have to do that.  Thak you TOM, I really appreciate this.  I'll buy you dinner.  As far as price though, 1300 for a salvaged 87gt?  Seem high to anyone else?  On the bright side, if I part it out.<P>I spoiler, good condition.<BR>2 mint 85 seats.<BR>120 mph speedo<BR>Tail lights in perfect shape.<BR>Nice tires<BR>Excelent stock rims<BR>Sub woofer and Slider in grey.<P>Ohh well, let me know if you think I should talk the guy down.  If so, to what?||||reg||1
Z||000005||la9||01-14-2000||01:03 PM||||If it was me I'd keep looking. Look at the list of what you know is wrong with it then double it for the things that you'll find wrong with it after you get it home. I'd offer him $500 and when he says "no" leave your number. Sometimes you will get the call back and if not I'm sure there is a much better deal out there. Unless you have a lot of time and $$$ for all the work you'll probably end up doing. Remember patience is a virtue, you can find a better deal.<BR>Almost forgot to add this. At least here in Ohio if you have a salvage title you will have to make sure everything works and have it inspected by the State Highway Patrol before you can get a title to drive it on the street. They also check #'s to make sure there are no stolen parts on it. If the car has been painted and the numbers have been painted over on the door even if it was the original they will confiscate it and you will have to buy a new one and show them the bill of sale. Also you have to pay for these inspections. It all sounds like too much trouble for anything but a parts car to me.<p>[This message has been edited by la9 (edited 01-14-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tom88gt||01-14-2000||01:45 PM||||I agree.  The salvage title is suspisious.  I have don't think the Salvation Army has anything to do with the car unless it was donated to them as a salvage.  <P>Typically, salvage vehicles were damaged so bad that the insurance company totaled the car and sold it to a junkyard for salvage value.  Someone probably found the car and bought it from the junkyard and had to apply for a new (salvage) title since the original title was "retired".  Each state is different so check with your local county court house or DMV for all the details.<P>I would not touch the car unless it was VERY cheap ($500 or less).  If the car was bad enough to be "totaled", then what surprizes remain to be found? ||||reg||1
Z||000007||GT Bastard||01-14-2000||04:08 PM||||I hate to disagree, but I'd jump at a deal like that where I live. Fiero's go very quickly here. There was a trashed '86 GT here that was missing body panels, needed a clutch, and needed paint and wheels for 600 bucks.  The funny thing was... It was gone immediately.  They go like crazy around here.  I think it sounds like a decent deal, but you might wanna make sure that one side on the nose isn't lower than the other(prob with my car right now) since it was hit. That would explain the missalignment, and it could be an expensive problem(as I am learning.)  Good luck!  Let us know the outcome.||||reg||1
Z||000008||WKDFIRO||01-15-2000||02:01 PM||||If you have a Fiero that has a bent frame, move on. In Calif. there are always other Fieros. Keep looking I say! Start off with a good Fiero and enhance it! They are still out there!<P>Besides, a "water pump problem" might be the beginning of a new engine if he has already overheated and cracked something. Save yourself the headache!||||reg||1
Z||000009||AL||01-16-2000||12:36 AM||||hey dis i paid 900 for my gt, and i had to go all the way out to universal studios,but my car didn't need all the stuff this one needs, your better of buying another one that doesn't have damage to the car,if memory serves me ther is a gt or se v6 in corona for 500 and it seems like it's a good car. look at the recycler's web and you will find it there, but if you do buy this other car and part it out i got first call on the tail lights..AL||||reg||1
Z||000010||DISenchanted||01-16-2000||06:19 AM||||Al, it's really funny that you mention Universal Studios.  This car is 2 miles from there.  Is the 86 a fast back?  I'll try to find recyclers web, but just in case.  Please send me the web address.  Thank you so much for your help.  You have no clue what this means to me.<P>DISenchanted||||reg||1
